AirymaxOS terminal entry points

  airy-os       OS identity, session state, desktop readiness
  airy-kernel   running kernel, build provenance, module count
  airy-bench    IPC round-trip latency and concurrency scaling
  airy-observe  machine-readable runtime snapshot, key=value lines
  airy-demo     one-screen summary recomputed from observe and bench
  airy-record   capture this terminal to a replayable log

Every value is printed as key=value and can be re-derived locally.

Cross-check the same machine with stock Linux tooling:

  uname -a                          running kernel, build time, machine
  cat /etc/os-release               distribution identity and version
  lscpu | head -12                  topology, model, cache
  free -h; lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,TYPE  memory and block devices
  ip -br addr                       interfaces and addresses
  systemd-analyze; systemctl --failed
  journalctl -b -p err --no-pager   boot errors, if any
